# UI Library & Styling Standards

## Core Technologies
- **Styling**: TailwindCSS (https://tailwindcss.com/)
- **Component Library**: spartan/ui (https://spartan.ng/) - The Angular implementation of Shadcn/UI.
- **Modals & Alerts**: SweetAlert2 (https://sweetalert2.github.io/)

## Development Rules

### 1. Component Selection
- Always prioritize **spartan/ui** components for layout, forms, and data display.
- Use **TailwindCSS** utility classes for all custom styling. Do not use inline styles or CSS modules unless strictly necessary.
- Use **SweetAlert2** for all user confirmations (deletions, warnings) and success/error notifications.

### 2. Angular & Spartan Integration
- Spartan uses **Brain** (logic) and **Helm** (directives/styling) modules. 
- Ensure that when generating components, you use the correct `@spartan-ng` imports.
- Follow the **Atomic Design** principle: keep components small and reusable.

### 3. Visual & Accessibility (WCAG)
- **Contrast**: Ensure all Tailwind color combinations meet WCAG AA standards.
- **Icons**: Use Lucide-Angular (default with Spartan) for all iconography.
- **Responsive**: Use a "Mobile-First" approach with Tailwind breakpoints (`sm:`, `md:`, `lg:`).

### 4. SweetAlert2 Usage
- Instead of native `window.confirm`, always use `Swal.fire()`.
- Create a reusable service in Angular to wrap SweetAlert2 calls for consistency across the app.

## Prohibited
- DO NOT use Bootstrap, Material UI, or PrimeNG.
- DO NOT use the React version of Shadcn/UI.
- DO NOT write vanilla CSS in `.css` or `.scss` files if it can be achieved with Tailwind.